{"The upsampling eligibility cache key uses Python's hash() of project_ids, which is process-randomized and can collide, leading to poor cache hit rates and ineffective invalidation across workers, causing inconsistent upsampling behavior and unnecessary cache growth in multi-process deployments": 0.9163147807121277, "OrganizationEventsStatsEndpoint._get_event_stats decides upsampling using the outer-scope request dataset, not the actual scoped_dataset being queried, so discover-split paths can incorrectly skip upsampling even when they run queries against discover/errors, yielding incorrect non-upsampled counts for allowlisted projects in split/fallback executions": 0.7246153354644775}